# ₊˚⊹ Activity 1: Presentation Design Principles ✦

## Project Overview

For this activity, I created a promotional poster design for **"Arrupe Hall Booth 7"**, featuring a free coffee booth event. The goal of this project was to apply fundamental presentation and graphic design principles to create a visually appealing and informative output.

The design focuses on presenting information in a creative yet organized manner while ensuring that important details such as the event name, date, location, and main message are easily recognized by the audience.

---

# Design Concept

The concept of the poster was inspired by the warm and comforting atmosphere associated with coffee. I used a coffee-themed design with warm tones, steam effects, and a minimalist layout to create a cozy and inviting visual experience.

The design aimed to capture the attention of viewers while clearly communicating the purpose of the event.

---

# Design Principles Applied

## Visual Hierarchy

Visual hierarchy was applied by arranging elements based on their level of importance.

The main title **"Arrupe Hall"** was placed prominently at the top to immediately introduce the event. The words **"Free Coffee"** were emphasized at the bottom because it serves as the main attraction that captures the audience's attention.

The date and event details were positioned in a clear area to allow viewers to easily identify important information.

---

## Contrast

Contrast was used through the combination of dark background colors and lighter text elements.

The difference between the background and typography helped important details stand out and improved readability. The use of warm coffee-related colors also strengthened the overall theme of the poster.

---

## Alignment

The elements were carefully arranged to create an organized and balanced composition.

The placement of the coffee cup, event details, and text followed a structured layout to prevent the design from appearing cluttered. Proper alignment helped guide the viewer's eyes naturally throughout the poster.

---

## Balance

Balance was achieved by distributing visual elements throughout the poster.

The coffee cup on one side was balanced by the text and event information on the other side, creating a stable and pleasing composition.

---

## Consistency

Consistency was maintained through the repeated use of coffee-inspired colors, typography styles, and visual elements.

The font choices and overall theme supported the message of the event and created a unified design.

---

## Simplicity

The design followed the principle of simplicity by focusing only on essential information.

Unnecessary elements were avoided to ensure that the audience could quickly understand the purpose of the poster without being overwhelmed by too much content.

---

# Creative Process

I started by identifying the purpose of the poster and determining the important information that needed to be presented.

After planning the layout, I selected appropriate colors, fonts, and visual elements that matched the coffee theme. I arranged the elements using design principles to improve readability and visual appeal.

The final output was refined by adjusting the placement, spacing, and emphasis of different elements to create a more organized and engaging design.

---

# Reflection

Through this activity, I learned that effective design is not only about making a presentation visually attractive but also about communicating information clearly.

I realized that every design element, including colors, fonts, images, and layout, has a purpose in guiding the audience's attention and improving understanding.

This activity helped me appreciate the importance of design principles in creating effective digital outputs. As a nursing student, these skills can be applied in creating educational materials, health promotions, and presentations that communicate important information in a clear and engaging way.

Overall, this activity improved my creativity, attention to detail, and understanding of how technology can support effective communication.
